    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP today, the offensive engine is anchored by **Corbin Carroll**, who leads all starters with an 81.24 efficiency score. Facing Bryce Elder, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a prime #2 slot in the lineup and a favorable matchup against a 4.40 xERA arm; his speed-first profile remains our most critical asset in the pursuit of SB volume. Behind him, **Max Muncy** (71.26) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (70.18) provide significant leverage in a smash spot against the struggling Cody Bradford. Both players see their scores buoyed by a 19% SP skill advantage and high park factors, making them high-upside plays despite lower projected spots in the batting order.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup today involved our middle infield depth, where **Cole Young** was the most notable exclusion from the active roster. **Cole Young** posted a 45.47 efficiency score against Hunter Brown, trailing behind the slightly more favorable situational matchups for **Travis Bazzana** and **Brice Turang**. While **Brice Turang** faces the daunting Tarik Skubal, the optimizer favors his 85% SB-delivery efficiency and superior platoon metrics, even with the suppressed raw score. Conversely, **Jose Caballero** remains on the roster despite a marginal 41.62 score; while his ceiling is currently capped by a difficult assignment against Cease, his speed profile dictates he maintains a spot to capitalize on any potential base-stealing opportunities late in the game.\n\nWe must remain cautious of the volatility inherent in our \"Lineup Pending\" designations, particularly regarding **Max Muncy**, **Brice Turang**, and **Tyler Soderstrom**. Should these players shift lower in their respective lineups, their efficiency scores will face downward pressure. Furthermore, **Austin Riley** (48.70) remains a peripheral play; his score is hampered by a #8 order designation that limits his RBI potential, and he is a primary candidate to be capped if we need to conserve game limits. With **James Wood** and **Giancarlo Stanton** confirmed on the IL, our current depth is focused entirely on maximizing the 5x5 categories through aggressive baserunning and high-park-factor matchups for **Mickey Moniak** and **Seiya Suzuki**.",
